{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfTh9Kd367SoNPnjHMyBP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Summary of Repository Findings:**\n\n- **Shipment.kt (line 9-14)**: Data class with status field using ShipmentStatus enum\n- **ShipmentStatus enum (line 23-27)**: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n- **ShipmentController.kt (line 22-56)**: Current endpoints are create, getById, list; uses resource location at RequestMapping(\"/shipments\")\n- **InMemoryShipmentRepository.kt (line 10-27)**: Provides save(), existsById(), findById(), findAll()\n- **ApiExceptions.kt (line 11-30)**: ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) are the patterns\n- **ErrorCode enum (line 31-37)**: Currently has SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS; no code for invalid state transitions\n- **GlobalExceptionHandler.kt (line 13-29)**: Converts ApiException to ApiError response body\n\n**Conventions the repository has:**\n1. POST endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...)` for creation\n2. Error handling uses sealed ApiException classes with HttpStatus and ErrorCode built-in\n3. All errors follow ApiError envelope format with error.code, error.message\n4. Tests use MockMvc with MockMvcRequestBuilders and MockMvcResultMatchers for assertions\n5. Controller methods throw exceptions for errors rather than returning error ResponseEntity\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add error code for shipment state conflicts\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add POST endpoint for confirm operation\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add tests for all four cases (CREATED->CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED idempotent, CANCELLED rejected, not found rejected)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Need to add a new ErrorCode enum value (this is necessary for API contract)\n2. Idempotent behavior requires checking if already CONFIRMED before rejecting\n3. Must ensure repository persistence is tested\n\n**Open questions:** None - the ticket is clear on all cases and the HTTP status codes are specified.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment, following the pattern of existing error codes that name the resource and the problem.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Takes a `@PathVariable shipmentId: String`\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code\n   - Return the shipment in ResponseEntity.ok()\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds with no change (idempotent)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with correct error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with correct error code\n\n**Rejected alternatives:**\n- Initially considered using a generic SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code, but SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM is more specific and follows the pattern of SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS.\n- Considered adding a service layer, but the existing architecture handles state transitions directly in the controller using the repository, so staying consistent with the create endpoint pattern is best.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path - CREATED → CONFIRMED:**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Controller: Retrieve S-1 from repository\n   - Controller: Check status is CREATED\n   - Controller: Create new Shipment with CONFIRMED status\n   - Repository: save() updates the in-memory store\n   - Response: 200 OK with Shipment body\n\n2. **Idempotent path - CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED:**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (shipment already CONFIRMED)\n   - Controller: Retrieve S-1 from repository\n   - Controller: Check status is CONFIRMED\n   - Controller: Do nothing (already in target state)\n   - Response: 200 OK with Shipment body (unchanged)\n\n3. **Conflict path - CANCELLED:**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (shipment CANCELLED)\n   - Controller: Retrieve S-1 from repository\n   - Controller: Check status is CANCELLED\n   - Controller: Throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler: Catch and convert to ApiError response\n   - Response: 409 Conflict with error envelope\n\n4. **Not found path:**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm\n   - Controller: findById returns null\n   - Controller: Throw ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler: Catch and convert to ApiError response\n   - Response: 404 Not Found with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Create shipment, confirm it, assert status changed to CONFIRMED and response is 200\n- Test 2: Create shipment, confirm twice, assert second confirm succeeds (200) and status remains CONFIRMED\n- Test 3: Write CANCELLED shipment directly to repository, attempt confirm, assert 409 with error.code = SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n- Test 4: Attempt confirm on non-existent ID, assert 404 with error.code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me implement the changes:\n\n**File 1: Update ApiError.kt to add the new error code**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1823,"cache_read_input_tokens":18635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1823},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":nul